                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b1c1615f-a45b-36a9-8942-1e8ed9afa774",
                        "entry_id": "b45acc81-2cba-3dd8-b104-3ff0894995c0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Indisputable, incontestable, unquestionable."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e94c70b2-e023-4b6e-84a2-6379922d98a4",
                                "sense_id": "b1c1615f-a45b-36a9-8942-1e8ed9afa774",
                                "text": "two inoppugnable reasons"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f3194a0f-4b61-480e-9ef9-c79e94c8e870",
                                "sense_id": "b1c1615f-a45b-36a9-8942-1e8ed9afa774",
                                "text": "Moreover, as this inoppugnable Propensity to Religion is a Cyon of God's own ingraffing on the Mind of Man, so also is it out of his power, tho' assisted by all the hellish Stratagems, totally to eradicate it thence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "37497cbb-61b0-4ce0-a83f-48d55963c5fa",
                                "sense_id": "b1c1615f-a45b-36a9-8942-1e8ed9afa774",
                                "text": "I am glad to see, in your account of miscellaneous reading, authors of such inoppugnable orthodoxy as Coleridge and Carlyle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a1f43c7-d34c-4dd8-b0b6-2141ec1b6c0c",
                                "sense_id": "b1c1615f-a45b-36a9-8942-1e8ed9afa774",
                                "text": "Do not argue with me. Argue with these stones. / Truth has no trouble in knowing itself. / That is it. The hard fact. The inoppugnable reality, / Here is something for you to digest. / Eat this and we'll see what appetite you have left / For a world hereafter."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2f2e7470-ddc8-3399-8195-88b405f946a4",
                        "entry_id": "b45acc81-2cba-3dd8-b104-3ff0894995c0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Insuperable, insurmountable."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "05336902-5a1a-4c3e-a8fa-28c43ced7adf",
                                "sense_id": "2f2e7470-ddc8-3399-8195-88b405f946a4",
                                "text": "… the disease … will be so violent and inoppugnable by the force of Nature, that the Temperament of Peters body … will thereby be dissolved, and so Death shall invevitably succeed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "95da24e5-9e82-4e89-b090-8242467ebd38",
                                "sense_id": "2f2e7470-ddc8-3399-8195-88b405f946a4",
                                "text": "The barrier vast and inoppugnable [sc. a mountain range]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
